"""Per-check prose: plain-words consequence, why it matters, fix, verify. Source for references/checks/*.md.

Format: ID: (in plain words, why it matters, fix, verify). Kept in one file so the catalog and the prose
can be reviewed together; tests/test_catalog_consistency.py asserts every catalog ID has an entry here.
"""
T = {
"SEC-001": ("An admin key for your backend is inside the code every visitor downloads, so anyone can read or change all your data.", "A key in the bundle is public. Admin keys bypass every access rule, so the whole database or payment account is exposed.", "Move the call behind a server route, action or edge function, read the key from a server-only variable, use the publishable key in the browser, then rotate the key.", "Re-run scan_secrets and scan_env; build the app and search the output for the key prefix; nothing must match."),
"SEC-002": ("A real key is saved in a file that is part of your repository, so anyone who can see the repository has it.", "For a public repository that means everyone; automated harvesters find keys within minutes.", "Remove the value, load it from the environment, ignore the file, keep an .env.example with empty values, and rotate the key. Removing it does not un-leak it.", "Scanner reports nothing in the tree; `git ls-files` lists no env file with values."),
"SEC-003": ("A key you deleted is still readable in your repository's history, to anyone who can clone it.", "Deleting a file in a later commit leaves the secret in history, forks and clones.", "Rotate the key first. Rewriting history is optional and disruptive; see owner-actions/purge-git-history.md.", "Owner confirms the old key no longer works. Close the finding as rotated, not removed."),
"SEC-004": ("Your .gitignore does not exclude .env files, so the next commit will publish your keys.", "Env files are where secrets live; the next `git add .` commits them.", "Add .env and .env.* (keeping !.env.example) to .gitignore, `git rm --cached` any tracked env file, add an .env.example.", "`git check-ignore .env` succeeds and `git ls-files` lists only example env files."),
"SEC-005": ("A variable meant to hold a secret has a name that makes the build tool copy it into the code sent to every visitor.", "Prefixes such as NEXT_PUBLIC_ and VITE_ exist precisely to inline the value into browser JavaScript.", "Rename it without the public prefix, move the code that uses it to the server, and rotate the key.", "Scanner clean; search the build output for the key prefix."),
"SEC-006": ("A key is typed directly into your source code, so it travels wherever the code goes.", "Source is copied, shared with AI tools, pushed and deployed; a literal secret travels with it.", "Replace the literal with an environment lookup validated at startup, then rotate the key.", "Scanner clean."),
"SEC-007": ("Your built website or source maps expose original code or a secret key to anyone who looks.", "Source maps reveal comments and sometimes inlined values; a key in the bundle is public.", "Disable public source maps or upload them privately to your error tracker, and remove any secret from client code.", "Config check passes and the build directory contains no secret."),
"SEC-008": ("There is no .env.example, so setting the app up elsewhere is guesswork and people paste real .env files into chats.", "Deployments fail in confusing ways and real secrets get shared to \"share the config\".", "Generate .env.example from the variables the code reads, empty values, marking which are server-only.", "Every variable read in code appears in the example."),
"SEC-009": ("Passwords, tokens or personal data are written to your logs, where many people and services can read them.", "Logs are widely readable, retained for long and forwarded to third parties.", "Remove the value or log an identifier instead of the credential.", "Scanner clean on the changed files."),
"SEC-010": ("The secret that signs login sessions is guessable or has a built-in fallback, so anyone can forge a login as any user.", "Whoever knows the secret can create a valid session for any account, including an administrator.", "Require the variable at startup with no fallback, generate a long random value, store it in the host's secret settings, rotate it.", "Scanner clean; the app refuses to start without the variable."),
"SEC-011": ("Test and live credentials are mixed, or one set is shared by all environments.", "Testing against production corrupts real data; shipping test keys means payments silently do nothing.", "Use separate projects or databases per environment and document which variables differ.", "Owner confirms separate values exist for production and preview."),
"SEC-012": ("A public key (maps, Firebase web key and similar) has no restrictions, so others can reuse it on their sites at your cost.", "Public keys are meant to be visible, but an unrestricted one can be billed to you.", "Restrict by HTTP referrer, app identifier and API scope in the provider console; set quotas and billing alerts.", "Owner confirms the restrictions."),
"SEC-013": ("Your AI provider key is usable from the browser or phone app, so anyone can copy it and spend your money.", "The key is extractable in seconds and usable for unlimited spend on your account.", "Create a server endpoint that holds the key, authenticates the caller and enforces limits; rotate the key; set a provider spending limit.", "Scanner clean; no provider host in the client bundle."),
"SEC-014": ("A secret is written into the mobile app's configuration, and anyone can download and unpack the app.", "App packages are downloadable and trivially unpacked.", "Move privileged calls to a backend and keep only public keys in the app; rotate the key.", "Scanner clean."),
"SEC-015": ("A private key or service account file is in your repository, so whoever has the repository can act as your service.", "It grants full impersonation of the service identity.", "Remove the file, ignore it, load it from secret storage, and revoke and reissue the key.", "Scanner clean; owner confirms revocation."),
"SEC-016": ("This is a public-by-design key (anon, publishable, Firebase web config). It is not a leak.", "These keys are meant to be in the browser; safety depends on the access rules behind them.", "Nothing to fix. Review the database checks instead.", "Not applicable."),
"AUTH-001": ("A page is hidden in the interface, but the data behind it can still be fetched directly by anyone.", "Hiding a screen does not protect data; anyone can call the endpoint or query the table.", "Enforce the rule on the server or in database policies; keep the UI check as a convenience.", "A request without a session to each data endpoint returns 401 or an empty result."),
"AUTH-002": ("Anyone on the internet can call this route; it reads or changes data and never checks who is asking.", "The route is callable by anyone and often runs with full database access.", "Check the session at the top of the handler and return 401 when missing, then check ownership (API-005).", "Scanner marks the route protected and a test without credentials gets 401."),
"AUTH-003": ("The login check in your middleware does not cover every route it is assumed to cover.", "A gap in the matcher is an open door, and frameworks have had middleware bypass bugs.", "Verify the session inside each handler or a shared data layer; keep middleware as an optimisation and keep the framework patched.", "Route inventory shows a per-handler check."),
"AUTH-004": ("The server believes whichever user ID the caller sends, so changing one field lets a person act as anyone.", "Identity read from the request is attacker-controlled.", "Derive identity only from the verified session on the server and ignore identity fields from the client.", "Test: signed in as A, send B's ID; get A's data or 403."),
"AUTH-005": ("The server trusts a login cookie or token it never verifies, so anyone can pose as another user.", "Unverified session data comes from something the visitor controls.", "Use the verifying call (getUser or getClaims for Supabase; jwt.verify with an algorithm allow-list for custom tokens).", "Scanner clean."),
"AUTH-006": ("The login token is stored where any script on the page can read it.", "One injected script or browser extension then means account takeover.", "Use HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite cookies on the web and secure storage on mobile.", "Cookie attributes present; scanner clean."),
"AUTH-007": ("The login cookie is missing protective flags, which makes it easier to steal or misuse.", "Without HttpOnly, Secure and SameSite it can be read by scripts, sent over plain HTTP or forged cross-site.", "Set httpOnly, secure and sameSite (use the __Host- prefix where possible).", "Scanner clean; response headers checked."),
"AUTH-008": ("People can sign up with an email address they do not own.", "Enables sign-up as someone else, invitation hijacking and account merging.", "Enable email confirmation and check email_verified before privileged actions and before linking identities.", "Dashboard shows it enabled."),
"AUTH-009": ("Weak passwords are allowed.", "Credential stuffing works against weak and reused passwords.", "Minimum length 8 or more, enable breach checking, offer social login or passkeys.", "Config or owner confirmation."),
"AUTH-010": ("Nothing limits how many times someone can try to sign in or guess a code.", "Enables password guessing, code brute force, email bombing and SMS cost attacks.", "Per-IP and per-account limits in a shared store, lockout with backoff, CAPTCHA on sign-up.", "Repeated attempts receive 429."),
"AUTH-011": ("The password reset flow can be abused to take over accounts.", "The reset flow is the easiest route to account takeover.", "Random single-use tokens with short expiry stored hashed, uniform responses, a fixed base URL from config.", "Tests for reuse, expiry and uniform response."),
"AUTH-012": ("After sign-in the app sends people wherever a link says, including to another website.", "Used for phishing and, in OAuth flows, token theft.", "Allow only same-origin relative paths (reject // and backslashes) or an explicit allow-list.", "Test with https://evil.example and //evil.example; both rejected."),
"AUTH-013": ("Users can grant themselves a role, plan or credits because it is stored where they can edit it.", "The user promotes themselves to administrator with one request.", "Store roles in server-controlled claims (app_metadata, custom claims) or a table users cannot write; restrict updatable columns.", "Test: an ordinary user tries to set the role and is denied."),
"AUTH-014": ("Sessions never expire, or signing out does not actually end them.", "A stolen token works forever.", "Short-lived access tokens with refresh rotation and server-side revocation on sign-out and password change.", "A token is rejected after sign-out."),
"AUTH-015": ("Another website can make a signed-in visitor's browser perform actions on your app.", "Cookie-authenticated state-changing requests need a forgery defence.", "SameSite cookies plus Origin or token validation; no state changes on GET.", "A cross-origin POST is rejected."),
"AUTH-016": ("Administrator accounts have no second factor.", "One phished admin password compromises all users.", "Enable MFA for admin roles or restrict admin access by SSO.", "Owner confirmation."),
"AUTH-017": ("A demo, seeded or shortcut login exists that anyone who reads the code can use.", "Published credentials and bypasses are the first thing attackers try.", "Remove them, restrict seeds to development, delete the accounts in production.", "Scanner clean; owner confirms accounts removed."),
"AUTH-018": ("Login tokens are checked too loosely, so forged or expired ones are accepted.", "Allows forged tokens.", "Pin algorithms, validate exp, iss and aud, and use the provider's verification library.", "Tests with a tampered and an expired token."),
"DB-001": ("Anyone on the internet can read and change every row in this table, because access rules are not switched on.", "With the public key that ships in every client, the auto-generated API exposes the whole table.", "Write a migration that enables RLS and adds least-privilege policies from assets/sql/ templates; you apply it.", "Scanner clean on migrations; the RLS test passes; an anonymous request returns no rows."),
"DB-002": ("A policy lets everyone read or change every row, so the access rule is on but protects nothing.", "RLS is technically enabled, but USING (true) opens the table.", "Scope to authenticated users and to the row owner or tenant; separate policies per operation.", "Scanner clean; the RLS test proves user A cannot read user B's rows."),
"DB-003": ("Any signed-up user can read or change every row; since anyone can sign up, that means anyone.", "Authenticated-only is not ownership.", "Add (select auth.uid()) = user_id or a tenant membership condition.", "Cross-user RLS test."),
"DB-004": ("A user can add rows that claim to belong to someone else, or hand their rows to another user.", "A missing or weak WITH CHECK lets ownership be forged. (PostgreSQL reuses USING for UPDATE and ALL when WITH CHECK is absent; the exposure is insert policies without it and weak explicit ones.)", "Add WITH CHECK mirroring the ownership condition; make ownership columns immutable where possible.", "Test: insert with another user's ID fails."),
"DB-005": ("A rule decides access from profile data users can edit themselves, so any user can grant themselves access.", "user_metadata is writable by the signed-in user.", "Use app_metadata or a roles table with its own policies.", "Scanner clean."),
"DB-006": ("A table has no column saying who owns each row, so no rule can keep users apart.", "Without an ownership column no rule can separate users; client-side filtering is a filter, not protection.", "Add the column with a default of the current user, backfill, then add policies.", "Migration present; cross-user test."),
"DB-007": ("A database function runs with full rights and anyone can call it through the API, skipping the access rules.", "SECURITY DEFINER functions run with their owner's rights and can bypass RLS for any caller.", "Move to a private schema or revoke EXECUTE from anon and public, set search_path = '', check auth.uid() inside.", "Scanner clean."),
"DB-008": ("A view shows rows to every caller regardless of the access rules on the tables behind it.", "By default a view runs with its creator's rights.", "Recreate with WITH (security_invoker = true) or move it out of the exposed schema.", "Scanner clean."),
"DB-009": ("Files in a storage bucket can be downloaded by anyone who has or guesses a link.", "A public bucket serves every uploaded file; listing may also be possible.", "Make the bucket private, add policies scoped by user folder, use short-lived signed URLs.", "Scanner clean; an anonymous fetch of a test object fails."),
"DB-010": ("Anyone on the internet can read and change your Firebase data without signing in.", "The whole database is readable and writable by anyone with the project ID, which is in the client.", "Deny by default, write per-collection rules scoped by request.auth.uid, keep rules in the repository and deploy them from it.", "Scanner clean; emulator rules tests added and passing."),
"DB-011": ("Any signed-up user can read or edit other people's Firebase data, or edit fields that should be server-controlled.", "A signed-in check without ownership or field validation is open to every user.", "Scope by request.auth.uid and validate writable fields with hasOnly; move privileged fields to server-written documents.", "Emulator tests for cross-user read, cross-user write and privileged field write."),
"DB-012": ("A database query is built by pasting request text into SQL, so a crafted input can read or destroy the whole database.", "SQL injection.", "Use parameterised queries or tagged templates and allow-list identifiers.", "Scanner clean; test with a quote character."),
"DB-013": ("The whole request body is written to the database, so the caller can set fields like role, owner or price.", "Mass assignment.", "Validate with a schema, pick allowed fields explicitly, set ownership from the session.", "Test: an extra privileged field in the body is ignored."),
"DB-014": ("Browser code connects straight to the database, which requires shipping the database password to every visitor.", "Full database credentials are published.", "Move data access behind server routes and rotate the database password.", "Scanner clean."),
"DB-015": ("The rules that protect your data exist only in a dashboard, so they cannot be reviewed, tested or restored from code.", "Security rules cannot be versioned or tested; this audit cannot see them.", "Pull the schema and policies into the repository with the vendor CLI and re-run the scan.", "Files present; scanner processes them."),
"DB-016": ("If data is lost or deleted, you may have no way to get it back.", "One bad migration, bug or attacker deletes everything permanently.", "Enable automated backups or point-in-time recovery, schedule an export, and perform one restore to a scratch project.", "Owner confirms the backup setting and one successful restore."),
"DB-017": ("The access rules will make every query slower as data grows.", "Unindexed policy columns and per-row auth.uid() calls cause full scans.", "Add indexes on policy columns and wrap auth.uid() in a sub-select.", "Scanner clean."),
"DB-018": ("Under real traffic the app will run out of database connections and go down.", "Serverless functions that open a connection per request exhaust the pool.", "Use the provider's pooler URL and one client instance per runtime.", "Config review."),
"DB-019": ("One customer may be able to see another customer's data.", "The worst incident for a B2B product.", "Enforce tenant membership in policies or a shared data layer; never accept a tenant ID without checking membership.", "Cross-tenant tests."),
"DB-020": ("Anyone can subscribe to live updates and watch private changes as they happen.", "Realtime follows the table's read rules and channel authorisation.", "Use private channels with authorisation and sound RLS; authorise socket rooms on the server.", "An unauthenticated subscription receives nothing."),
"DB-021": ("Visitors who are not signed in have broad database grants.", "Grants plus a permissive policy expose data to anonymous callers.", "Revoke, grant minimal rights, check auth.uid() in functions.", "Scanner clean."),
"DB-022": ("Record IDs are guessable, which makes enumeration trivial where authorisation is weak.", "Random IDs mitigate but do not fix missing authorisation.", "Fix authorisation first, then consider UUIDs for public identifiers.", "See API-005."),
"DB-023": ("The app connects to the database as a superuser, so any bug has unlimited reach and RLS is skipped.", "A least-privilege role limits the blast radius.", "Create a dedicated least-privilege application role.", "Owner confirms the connection user changed."),
"DB-024": ("Anyone, or any signed-up user, can download every user's private details such as email or phone.", "Mass scraping of personal data.", "Split public and private columns into separate tables or expose a restricted view; select explicit columns.", "Anonymous and cross-user reads return only public columns."),
"API-001": ("The route uses what the caller sends without checking its type or size.", "Unexpected types and sizes cause crashes, bad data and injection paths.", "Validate at the boundary with a schema, reject with 400, use only the parsed result.", "Test with a wrong type and an oversized string."),
"API-002": ("Nothing limits how often costly endpoints can be called, so one script can run up bills or take the app down.", "Exhausted quotas and surprise costs.", "Add limits backed by a shared store or the platform firewall, stricter on costly endpoints.", "A test receives 429 after the threshold."),
"API-003": ("Any website can make requests to your API as the signed-in visitor and read the answers.", "Wildcard or reflected origins with credentials defeat the browser's protection.", "Use an explicit origin allow-list from configuration; credentials only for those origins.", "Scanner clean; a request from a disallowed origin is refused."),
"API-004": ("When something fails, the server sends internal error text to the caller.", "Leaks schema, file paths and sometimes secrets.", "Return a generic message plus a request ID; send details to logs and the error tracker.", "A forced error shows no internals."),
"API-005": ("A signed-in user can change the ID in a request and read or change someone else's record.", "Insecure direct object reference, the most common serious flaw in AI-built backends.", "Put the ownership condition in the query itself and return 404 on mismatch.", "Test: user A requests user B's resource and gets 404."),
"API-006": ("The server fetches any web address the caller supplies, which lets outsiders reach internal systems through your server.", "Server-side request forgery.", "Allow-list hosts, or block private, loopback and link-local ranges, forbid redirects to them, require https, set timeouts and size limits.", "Tests with http://169.254.169.254/, http://localhost and a redirecting URL."),
"API-007": ("Anyone can send fake events to a webhook and the app believes them.", "Forged \"payment succeeded\" or \"user created\" events.", "Verify the signature with the provider's library against the raw body and check the timestamp tolerance.", "An unsigned payload returns 400."),
"API-008": ("A list endpoint returns every row with no limit, which gets slow and hands scrapers a bulk export.", "Slow responses, large bills and easy data export.", "Enforce a maximum page size on the server and paginate with a cursor.", "A huge limit request is capped."),
"API-009": ("The server accepts very large request bodies, so a few requests can exhaust memory.", "Memory exhaustion and cost.", "Use small per-route limits; larger only for streaming upload routes.", "An oversized request returns 413."),
"API-010": ("A server action or procedure changes data without checking who calls it; every action is a public address.", "Each is an HTTP endpoint regardless of where its button is rendered.", "Authenticate and authorise inside every action; validate arguments.", "Direct invocation without a session fails."),
"API-011": ("The GraphQL API publishes its schema and accepts arbitrarily deep queries.", "Schema discovery and expensive nested queries.", "Disable introspection and the playground in production for a private API, add depth and cost limits, authorise in resolvers.", "Config check."),
"API-012": ("A leftover developer endpoint is part of the app; tools for the developer are tools for an attacker.", "Debug routes can dump environment variables or run queries.", "Delete it, or guard with an environment check and admin authorisation.", "Scanner clean."),
"API-013": ("A server function accepts calls from anyone with no sign-in check, while holding privileged credentials.", "The function is a public endpoint.", "Enable JWT verification or verify the token in code; verify signatures for webhooks.", "Scanner clean; an unauthenticated call returns 401."),
"API-014": ("Anyone can start a scheduled job by visiting its address, as often as they like.", "Batch jobs, emails and billing runs can be triggered repeatedly.", "Require the platform's cron secret header or a signed token; make jobs idempotent.", "A call without the secret returns 401."),
"API-015": ("A file path is built from what the caller sends, so `../` can reach files such as your secret settings.", "Path traversal.", "Resolve against a base directory and verify the result stays inside; prefer IDs mapped to stored paths.", "Test with ../../.env."),
"API-016": ("What the caller sends reaches a shell or code interpreter, letting an attacker run commands on your server.", "Remote code execution: complete server takeover.", "Avoid shells, pass argument arrays, allow-list commands, use safe parsers.", "Scanner clean."),
"API-017": ("Retries or double clicks can create duplicate orders, charges or messages.", "Duplicate charges, orders and deductions.", "Idempotency keys with a unique constraint; disable the button while pending as a convenience.", "The same request twice produces one effect."),
"API-018": ("A route changes data on a plain link visit or accepts the wrong HTTP method.", "Crawlers, link previews and image tags can trigger it.", "Restrict to the intended method and return 405 otherwise.", "A request with the wrong method is refused."),
"API-019": ("The response includes more fields than the page needs, such as password hashes or other users' emails.", "Data leaks through the network tab.", "Select explicit fields or use response schemas.", "A test asserts sensitive fields are absent."),
"PAY-001": ("The buyer's browser decides the price or plan, so anyone can pay what they like.", "The buyer sets their own price.", "The client sends only product or plan identifiers; the server maps them to prices it controls and recomputes totals.", "A tampered amount is ignored or rejected."),
"PAY-002": ("Anyone can send a fake \"payment succeeded\" message and get paid access for free.", "A forged event grants paid access.", "Verify with the provider library and the raw body; use separate secrets per environment.", "An unsigned event returns 400."),
"PAY-003": ("Opening the success page grants paid access without any payment.", "Real payments that complete after the tab closes are also lost.", "Grant entitlements in the verified webhook; the success page only displays status.", "Hitting the success URL without payment changes nothing."),
"PAY-004": ("Payment events can arrive twice or out of order, giving double credits or wrong states.", "Providers retry and reorder events.", "Store processed event IDs with a unique constraint; set state from the provider's current object.", "Replaying the same event has no extra effect."),
"PAY-005": ("Paid features are locked only in the interface, so free users can call them directly.", "Server endpoints for paid features must check entitlement.", "Check entitlement on the server for every paid action; store it in server-written data.", "A free user receives 402 or 403."),
"PAY-006": ("Cancelled, refunded or failed subscriptions may keep access, or paying customers may lose it.", "Only the first checkout event is handled.", "Handle renewal failure, cancellation, refund, dispute, plan change and trial end; derive access from current status.", "Fixture-event tests for each transition."),
"PAY-007": ("A user can put someone else's customer or subscription ID into a billing request and open or change their billing.", "Identifiers must come from the session user's record.", "Look up customer and subscription IDs on the server for the signed-in user.", "Cross-user test."),
"PAY-008": ("The wrong payment mode is configured: test keys in production or live keys in development.", "Launching with test keys means no revenue; developing with live keys means real charges.", "Correct per-environment keys; restricted keys in production.", "Owner confirms, then one real low-value transaction end to end, refunded."),
"PAY-009": ("Card numbers pass through your own server, putting you in the strictest card-security scope.", "A breach would be catastrophic.", "Use the provider's hosted checkout or embedded elements.", "Scanner clean."),
"PAY-010": ("Concurrent requests can spend the same credit many times.", "Read-then-write balance updates are not atomic.", "Use an atomic conditional update or a transaction with locking, plus a check constraint against negatives.", "N parallel requests with balance 1 produce exactly one success."),
"PAY-011": ("Money is stored or computed as a decimal-inexact number, so totals can be off by a cent.", "Rounding errors in totals, tax and refunds.", "Use integer minor units or decimal types end to end.", "Schema and code review."),
"UP-001": ("Uploads of any size and type are accepted.", "Storage cost abuse, malware hosting and executable content on your domain.", "Enforce size and type on the server or in storage policy and verify magic bytes.", "Tests with an oversized file and a disallowed type."),
"UP-002": ("Uploaded files are served from your own domain as live content, so an uploaded HTML or SVG file can run scripts.", "Stored cross-site scripting.", "Serve from a separate storage domain, force download for non-images, sanitise or rasterise SVG.", "An uploaded HTML file does not render on your origin."),
"UP-003": ("Files are stored under the name the uploader chose, so uploads can overwrite each other or escape the folder.", "Overwriting other users' files and path traversal.", "Generate random keys on the server under a per-user prefix.", "Writing under another user's prefix fails."),
"UP-004": ("Private files are shared through permanent public links.", "Anyone with or guessing the link has the file forever.", "Keep objects private and issue short-lived signed URLs after an authorisation check.", "An anonymous fetch of the stored URL fails."),
"UP-005": ("One account can run up your storage and bandwidth bill.", "No per-user quota.", "Track usage and enforce quotas when issuing upload URLs.", "Exceeding the quota is refused."),
"UP-006": ("A crafted image or document can take the server down.", "Decompression bombs and parser vulnerabilities.", "Limit dimensions and duration, set timeouts, isolate workers, keep libraries updated.", "Config review."),
"LLM-001": ("Anyone can use your AI feature without an account, and you pay for it.", "A free AI proxy at your expense, discovered and abused quickly.", "Require a session; for public demos add strict limits, a CAPTCHA and a hard budget.", "An unauthenticated call returns 401."),
"LLM-002": ("Nothing caps AI usage per user, so one user or a loop can produce an unbounded bill.", "No per-user limit or spending cap.", "Per-user quotas on the server, request rate limits, a provider budget with alerts.", "Quota test; owner confirms the provider budget."),
"LLM-003": ("The browser chooses the model, system prompt or parameters of your AI call.", "Users pick the most expensive model, remove guardrails or use your endpoint as a general proxy.", "The server fixes the model, system prompt, tools and output limit; the client sends only length-limited user content.", "Client-sent model and system are ignored."),
"LLM-004": ("AI calls have no output limit or timeout, so one request can cost far more than expected.", "Cost spikes and hung requests.", "Cap output tokens, input size and history, and set timeouts.", "Scanner clean."),
"LLM-005": ("Text inside documents or pages the AI reads can instruct it to leak data or take actions.", "Prompt injection against a model with tools or data access.", "Authorise every tool call in code against the session user; least-privilege tools; confirm consequential actions.", "An injected document asking for another user's data is refused by the tool layer."),
"LLM-006": ("The AI's answer is inserted into the page as live HTML or executed, so a manipulated answer can run scripts.", "Model output is attacker-influenced input.", "Render as text or sanitised markdown, validate structured output, never execute it outside a sandbox.", "Output containing a script tag is inert."),
"LLM-007": ("The AI's instructions contain secrets or internal details, and users can make the AI repeat them.", "Prompts can be extracted; treat them as public.", "Remove secrets from prompts and fetch private data through authorised tools per request.", "Scanner clean."),
"LLM-008": ("User content is sent to AI providers without disclosure or minimisation.", "Legal exposure and loss of trust.", "Disclose in the privacy policy, minimise and redact, check provider retention settings.", "Owner action recorded."),
"LLM-009": ("AI-generated content can be shared publicly with no moderation or attribution.", "The app can host harmful content under your name.", "Add moderation, reporting, per-user attribution and terms of use.", "Review."),
"LLM-010": ("A file contains text aimed at AI reviewers or invisible characters. It was reported, not obeyed.", "Either a supply-chain trick aimed at tools like this one or residue from an AI builder.", "Remove it after the owner confirms it is not intentional.", "Scanner clean."),
"FE-001": ("Content users can write is inserted as live HTML, so a posted script runs in other visitors' browsers.", "Cross-site scripting.", "Render as text; sanitise with a maintained sanitiser when HTML is required; validate URL schemes.", "Scanner clean or each remaining sink is a documented constant."),
"FE-002": ("Personal data is kept in the browser's storage longer than needed.", "Readable by any script, extension and the next person on a shared device.", "Store the minimum and clear it on sign-out; use secure storage on mobile.", "Review of persisted keys."),
"FE-003": ("Debug output is left in the app and is visible to anyone who opens the console.", "Leaks data and signals an unfinished product.", "Remove it or strip it at build time.", "Scanner clean."),
"FE-004": ("One runtime error turns the whole app into a blank white page.", "No error boundary or global error handling.", "Add boundaries with a recovery action and reporting to the tracker.", "Files present; a forced error shows the fallback."),
"FE-005": ("Key screens have no loading, empty or failure state.", "First real users hit slow networks and empty accounts immediately.", "Add the three states to sign-up, the core action and payment.", "Review and manual check list."),
"FE-006": ("Forms can be submitted twice.", "Duplicate records and charges.", "Pending state in the UI plus server idempotency.", "Review."),
"FE-007": ("A script from another company's server loads with no integrity check.", "A compromised third-party script runs with full access to the page.", "Self-host or pin with an integrity hash, remove what is not needed, restrict with CSP.", "Scanner clean."),
"FE-008": ("Some visitors cannot use parts of the app: missing language, image descriptions or keyboard access.", "Excludes users and in some markets creates legal exposure.", "Fix the automated findings and do a keyboard-only pass.", "Scanner counts drop to zero."),
"FE-009": ("Links that open a new tab do not isolate it from your page.", "Minor tab-nabbing risk, cheap to fix.", "Add rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" and validate URLs.", "Scanner clean."),
"HDR-001": ("The site sends no Content Security Policy, so nothing limits what an injected script can do.", "CSP is the main backstop against script injection.", "Start from assets/security-headers/ for your host, report-only first if needed, then tighten.", "Config present; optional probe shows the header."),
"HDR-002": ("Nothing makes browsers insist on HTTPS, so a visitor on a hostile network can be downgraded.", "Allows downgrade to an unencrypted connection.", "Add HSTS once HTTPS works everywhere and redirect HTTP to HTTPS.", "Config or probe."),
"HDR-003": ("Other sites can embed your pages in an invisible frame and trick visitors into clicking.", "Clickjacking.", "frame-ancestors 'none' or 'self' unless embedding is a feature.", "Config or probe."),
"HDR-004": ("Small free protections (nosniff, referrer and permissions policies) are not switched on.", "Prevents content-type confusion and URL leakage.", "Add them from the template.", "Config or probe."),
"HDR-005": ("A page or response that depends on who is signed in may be cached and served to someone else.", "One user's page is served to another.", "Cache-Control: private, no-store for personalised responses; mark dynamic routes dynamic.", "Test two sessions against the same URL."),
"HDR-006": ("The server announces which framework it runs.", "A minor information leak, trivial to remove.", "Disable the X-Powered-By header.", "Config."),
"DEP-001": ("The app runs in development or debug mode in production.", "Debug modes expose stack traces and dev servers are slow and unsafe.", "Use proper build and start commands; debug flags default off.", "Scanner clean; production start command documented."),
"DEP-002": ("Production and development share one backend, so experiments run against real users' data.", "A bad migration is immediately a production outage.", "Separate projects or databases; previews use the development backend.", "Owner confirms; env files differ."),
"DEP-003": ("The app reads its settings in many places without validating them at startup.", "A missing variable becomes a confusing failure or a silent insecure fallback.", "One module that validates the environment with a schema and fails fast.", "Starting without a required variable fails with a clear error."),
"DEP-004": ("Monitors cannot tell whether the app is alive.", "No health check endpoint.", "Add a cheap endpoint that returns status without details.", "Endpoint returns 200."),
"DEP-005": ("If a release breaks, recovery takes as long as debugging under pressure.", "No known rollback path.", "Document the host's instant rollback; keep migrations backward compatible for one release.", "Runbook section exists."),
"DEP-006": ("Tomorrow's deployment may install different code than today's.", "No lockfile, mixed package managers, unpinned versions or runtime.", "One package manager, a committed lockfile, a pinned runtime, clean-install commands.", "Scanner clean."),
"DEP-007": ("Old preview or staging copies of the app stay public and may be indexed.", "They may reach production data and are unpatched.", "Enable deployment protection, point previews at development data, unpublish stale previews.", "Owner confirmation."),
"DEP-008": ("The build ignores type and lint errors, so real bugs ship unnoticed.", "AI builders often switch these flags on to make a build pass.", "Turn the flags off, fix what surfaces, enable strict mode gradually.", "The build passes without the flags."),
"DEP-009": ("The container image runs as root or bakes in secrets.", "Secrets live forever in image layers and root widens any compromise.", "Multi-stage build, non-root user, .dockerignore, runtime secrets, pinned base image.", "Scanner clean."),
"DEP-010": ("Function region or timeouts do not match the database or the work.", "Slow responses and random timeouts.", "Co-locate regions; stream or move long work to background jobs.", "Config review."),
"DEP-011": ("The project lives only inside the AI builder, so you cannot back up, audit or move it.", "You depend on one vendor for recovery.", "Connect to your own GitHub repository; own the backend project and domain; document how to build and deploy.", "Owner confirmation; remote present."),
"DEP-012": ("Reloading or sharing a link to an inner page shows the host's 404.", "Single-page apps need a host rewrite to index.html.", "Add the pages and rewrite rules for your host.", "Files and rewrite config present."),
"DEP-013": ("Anyone, including an AI agent, can push straight to the branch that deploys.", "An unreviewed change goes straight to production.", "Branch protection with required checks; agents work on branches.", "Owner confirmation."),
"DEP-014": ("A loop or abuse can become a surprise bill before anyone notices.", "No budgets or alerts on pay-per-use services.", "Budgets, hard caps where offered, and alerts at several thresholds per provider.", "Owner confirmation per provider."),
"DEPS-001": ("A package you use has a known security hole that attackers scan for.", "Known vulnerabilities in frameworks and auth libraries are exploited at scale.", "Update to patched versions, prioritising framework, auth, database and parsing libraries; test after each.", "Audit shows no high or critical advisories for production dependencies."),
"DEPS-002": ("Your framework version no longer receives security fixes.", "New vulnerabilities will never be patched.", "Plan the upgrade; apply the latest patch of the current major now.", "Version bump present; build passes."),
"DEPS-003": ("A package is imported but not declared, or its name looks like a misspelling of a popular one; invented names can be registered by attackers.", "AI tools sometimes invent package names.", "Replace with the intended real package after checking its registry page, and remove look-alikes.", "Scanner clean."),
"DEPS-004": ("A listed package is never used.", "Each dependency is attack surface and upgrade work.", "Remove it after confirming the build passes.", "Build passes."),
"DEPS-005": ("A development tool ships to production, or a runtime package is dev-only.", "Larger attack surface, or a production crash on a missing module.", "Move entries to the right section.", "Clean production install and start."),
"DEPS-006": ("Nothing tells you when a new security fix is released for your packages.", "Vulnerabilities announced after launch go unnoticed.", "Add Dependabot or Renovate with grouped weekly updates.", "File present."),
"DEPS-007": ("A dependency's licence may oblige you to publish your code or forbid commercial use.", "Legal exposure for a commercial product. This is not legal advice.", "Flag it for the owner's decision and consider alternatives.", "Owner decision recorded."),
"PRIV-001": ("The app collects accounts but has no privacy policy or terms.", "Required by law in most markets, by app stores, payment providers and sign-in screens.", "Add pages linked from sign-up and the footer; draft a factual data inventory for your lawyer. This is not legal advice.", "Pages exist and are linked."),
"PRIV-002": ("Tracking scripts load before visitors are asked.", "Regulatory exposure and ad-platform policy violations where consent is required.", "Gate non-essential scripts behind consent or use privacy-friendly analytics.", "Scripts absent before consent."),
"PRIV-003": ("Users cannot delete their account or export their data.", "A legal right in many regions and an app store requirement.", "A deletion endpoint that removes rows, files and third-party records, with a confirmation step and a data export.", "After deletion no rows or objects for the user remain."),
"PRIV-004": ("Personal data appears in logs, analytics events or error reports.", "Copies spread to systems with weaker controls and longer retention.", "Log IDs, scrub in the tracker's before-send hook, mask inputs in session replay.", "Scanner clean; tracker configuration reviewed."),
"PRIV-005": ("Sensitive data is stored unprotected, or passwords use a fast hash.", "A breach causes real harm to people and severe consequences for you.", "Collect less; use argon2id, scrypt or bcrypt; encrypt sensitive fields; get a professional audit for regulated data.", "Scanner clean; schema review."),
"PRIV-006": ("You need a list of outside services that receive your users' data.", "For the privacy policy, customer questionnaires and incident response.", "Copy the generated inventory into the report appendix and complete it.", "Inventory present."),
"PRIV-007": ("Session recording captures what users type.", "Passwords and private messages end up in a third party's recordings.", "Mask all inputs by default and exclude sensitive pages.", "Configuration review."),
"PRIV-008": ("Old data is kept forever.", "Old data is pure liability.", "Define retention periods and add cleanup jobs.", "Jobs or policies present."),
"OBS-001": ("If the app breaks for a user, you will not find out.", "The owner learns about failures from angry users, or never.", "Add a tracker on client and server with release tagging, personal data scrubbing and private source maps.", "A test error appears in the tracker."),
"OBS-002": ("Errors are swallowed or logs are unusable, so incidents cannot be investigated.", "Attacks leave no trace.", "Structured logs with request ID, route, status, duration and user ID; never secrets; handle or rethrow every caught error.", "Sample log line reviewed; empty catch blocks removed."),
"OBS-003": ("Downtime can go unnoticed for hours.", "No uptime monitoring or alerting.", "An external check on the health endpoint and main page, alerting a channel someone watches.", "Owner confirmation."),
"OBS-004": ("After an incident nobody can say who did what.", "No audit trail for sensitive actions.", "An append-only server-written audit table: actor, action, target, time, request ID.", "Table and write calls present."),
"OBS-005": ("You cannot tell whether launch is working.", "No visibility into sign-up, activation and payment.", "A handful of server-side events for the key steps.", "Events visible."),
"OBS-006": ("The first incident will be handled by improvisation.", "No runbook.", "A one-page RUNBOOK.md: hosting, rollback, key rotation, restore, contacts, user notification.", "RUNBOOK.md exists."),
"REL-001": ("Operations fail silently and the screen shows success.", "Unawaited promises, ignored errors and unchecked responses.", "Await and check; surface errors to the user and the tracker.", "Scanner clean on changed files."),
"REL-002": ("A slow outside service can hang every request.", "No timeouts or retry policy on external calls.", "Timeouts on every external call; bounded retries with backoff for idempotent operations only.", "Review."),
"REL-003": ("A failure part-way through a multi-step write leaves inconsistent data.", "No transaction around related writes.", "Use a database transaction or a single database function.", "A forced failure at the second step leaves no partial data."),
"REL-004": ("State kept in server memory disappears or differs between instances.", "In-memory rate limits do not limit on serverless.", "Use a shared store such as the database or a key-value service.", "Scanner clean."),
"REL-005": ("Long work runs inside a request and can time out or be duplicated.", "Timeouts, lost work and duplicated work on retry.", "Use a queue or background function with status polling; make jobs idempotent.", "Review."),
"REL-006": ("Dates are handled in local time, causing off-by-one-day bugs.", "A large share of the world's users are affected.", "Store UTC with zone-aware types and convert at the edges.", "Tests around midnight and daylight saving changes."),
"REL-007": ("An untested backup is a hope, not a backup.", "Nobody has restored one.", "Perform one restore into a scratch environment and record the steps and time taken.", "Owner confirmation with a date."),
"REL-008": ("A non-essential outside service can take down sign-in or checkout.", "Hard dependency on one third party with no fallback.", "Load non-essential services asynchronously and fail open.", "Blocking the vendor host leaves the core flow working."),
"PERF-001": ("The code asks the database one question per item, so pages slow to seconds with real data.", "N+1 queries.", "Batch with `in`, joins or includes.", "Query count drops; scanner clean."),
"PERF-002": ("The app downloads a whole table and filters it in the browser.", "Slow, expensive, and hands visitors rows they should not receive.", "Filter, sort and paginate in the query.", "The network response contains only the needed page."),
"PERF-003": ("Large images slow the first load on phones.", "Where most launch traffic is lost.", "Resize, compress, use modern formats and lazy loading.", "Asset sizes under thresholds."),
"PERF-004": ("A large JavaScript bundle slows interaction on mid-range phones.", "Whole libraries imported for one function.", "Per-module imports, dynamic import for heavy features, remove unused libraries.", "Bundle size report before and after."),
"PERF-005": ("Public pages are rendered on every visit although they are the same for everyone.", "Unnecessary cost and fragility under a traffic spike.", "Static generation or revalidation for public pages; immutable caching for hashed assets.", "Config review."),
"PERF-006": ("Live subscriptions are opened and never closed.", "Memory leaks, duplicate events and growing read costs.", "Unsubscribe in cleanup and narrow the listener's query.", "Scanner clean."),
"MAIL-001": ("Your verification and reset emails may land in spam or be rejected.", "The sending domain lacks SPF, DKIM and DMARC.", "Configure the records with your email provider (owner-actions/dns-and-email.md).", "Records present; a test email passes authentication."),
"MAIL-002": ("Sign-up emails use the backend's test mail service, which is tightly rate limited.", "Built-in senders are for testing; sign-ups fail once real traffic arrives.", "Configure a transactional email provider as custom SMTP and brand the templates.", "Owner confirmation."),
"MAIL-003": ("Links in emails, sign-in and payment redirects point to localhost or a preview address.", "They break in production.", "Build the base URL from environment and update provider dashboards with the production domain.", "Scanner clean; owner confirms dashboards."),
"MAIL-004": ("Anyone can make the app send email or text messages to any address.", "The app becomes a spam cannon; SMS fraud costs real money.", "Authenticate where possible, rate limit per IP, account and recipient, CAPTCHA on public forms, fixed templates.", "Limit test."),
"MAIL-005": ("Marketing email has no unsubscribe.", "A legal requirement in many regions and a deliverability requirement.", "Add unsubscribe handling and honour it.", "Review."),
"TEST-001": ("There are no automated tests, so any later change can silently break sign-up or payment.", "Especially risky with AI-agent edits.", "Add a small set: sign-in, the core action, cross-user denial, payment webhook handling.", "Tests run and pass in CI."),
"TEST-002": ("Nothing tests the access rules, which are your main security boundary.", "One edit can open the database.", "Generate tests from assets/sql/rls_test.sql.tmpl or emulator rule tests.", "Tests pass and fail when a policy is deliberately loosened."),
"TEST-003": ("Nothing checks changes before they go live.", "Broken and insecure changes ship unchecked.", "Install assets/ci/prodready.yml and add install, typecheck, test, build and audit steps.", "The workflow runs green."),
"TEST-004": ("Your repository does not block the next leaked key before it is pushed.", "Secret scanning and push protection prevent leaks.", "Enable secret scanning and push protection; optional pre-commit hook.", "Owner confirmation."),
"LAUNCH-001": ("Shared links show a default title, description or someone else's image.", "Default or missing page metadata.", "Set title, description, canonical URL and social image.", "Scanner clean."),
"LAUNCH-002": ("The app's icons or web manifest are still the template's or missing.", "A visible sign of an unfinished product.", "Replace with your own assets.", "Scanner clean."),
"LAUNCH-003": ("Search engines get no guidance, or are told to ignore the site.", "Missing or wrong robots and sitemap.", "Correct robots rules and sitemap; noindex non-production environments.", "Scanner clean."),
"LAUNCH-004": ("Placeholder content or fake testimonials are still in the app.", "Destroys credibility; invented statistics can be unlawful advertising.", "Replace or remove; wire or remove dead controls.", "Scanner clean."),
"LAUNCH-005": ("The AI builder's badge, scripts or default README are still in the app.", "Unprofessional, and some scaffolding adds scripts you do not control.", "Remove where your plan permits and replace the README.", "Scanner clean."),
"LAUNCH-006": ("Users cannot get help or report a security problem.", "Problems go unreported or are reported publicly.", "Add a support email or form and a security.txt.", "Present."),
"LAUNCH-007": ("Domain, redirects or certificates are not finalised.", "Duplicate hosts split cookies and rankings; auth callbacks fail on the wrong host.", "Choose a canonical host, redirect the other, update every provider's allowed URL list.", "Owner confirmation."),
"LAUNCH-008": ("App store requirements are not met yet.", "Store rejection delays launch by days or weeks.", "Add permission descriptions, real bundle identifiers, HTTPS-only traffic and in-app account deletion.", "Scanner clean for the automated items."),
"LAUNCH-009": ("There is no README explaining how to run and deploy the app.", "Nobody else, including a future AI agent, can work on it safely.", "Write what the app is, the stack, how to run it, environment variables, how to deploy, and where data lives.", "File present and accurate."),
"LAUNCH-010": ("A brand-new user's first run has never been tried on production.", "The first real user hits the path the builder never tested.", "Run a ten-step manual smoke test on the production deployment before announcing.", "Owner confirms completion."),
}

